[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two shallow matte ceramic bowls containing balsamic-seared mahi-mahi fillets served over a warm bed of brown lentils and quinoa. The primary bowl is centered in the frame, 3/4 overhead at a 40-degree angle, with the second bowl softly blurred in the background. The mahi-mahi fillets are golden-brown with visible seasoning grains of garlic powder and oregano, placed directly beside the quinoa-lentil mixture rather than on top. The base consists of a hearty blend of quinoa, tender brown lentils, and wilted, dark green baby spinach, all coated in a rich, dark amber balsamic reduction. Blistered cherry tomatoes, partially burst and caramelized, are tucked throughout the grain base. A shallow depth of field keeps the main fillet sharp while the background fades into a natural bokeh. Lighting is soft, directional natural light from a window on the left, casting subtle shadows and creating a slight sheen on the balsamic glaze. The setting is a rustic, aged oak wooden table with subtle imperfections. Props include a single wooden spoon resting naturally on the linen napkin beside the bowl and a few scattered brown lentils on the wood surface. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, authentic. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric garnish placement, a small balsamic reduction drip on the plate rim, slightly uneven browning on the fish. Include subtle traces of the cooking process: a few tiny grains of quinoa on the table, a slight oil mark near the plate. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces."
]
